# Agent Environment

This repository uses **har** for isolated agent development. Each coding agent gets its own ports, database, and processes.

## Start here

1. Read [`.har/README.md`](.har/README.md) — what the harness contains and how to run it
2. Read [`.har/CLAUDE.agent.md`](.har/CLAUDE.agent.md) — detailed instructions for your agent slot

## Commands

```bash
./.har/setup-infra.sh          # Shared Docker + template DB (once)
./.har/launch.sh 1             # Launch agent slot 1
./.har/agent-cli.sh 1 status   # Check running processes
./.har/verify.sh 1             # Verify after changes
./.har/teardown.sh 1           # Tear down when done
```

## Rules

- Use `./.har/agent-cli.sh <id> ...` for all environment operations
- Do not hardcode ports — use env vars from `.env.agent.<id>`
- Do not run raw `docker compose` for shared infra
- Do not touch other agents' databases or PM2 processes
- Run `./.har/verify.sh <id> --full` before declaring work complete

